y pacing that myself even as I  grow my business which is about how I  spend my day I'm a big believer in  Chungking your time and I think a lot of  people get distracted and I was to buy  new things coming in emails tweets  Facebook updates and you spend so much  time reacting to these things and  putting out fires that you don't  actually get into spend any time with I  call CEO time or you're building your  business and working on it instead of in  it so I like chunky  time and basically that that concept is  finding things that you do on a regular  basis and doing them all at once so if  you do something multiple times a day  like check email for example then do  that once a day if you do things  multiple times a week like maybe meet  people then try to do that once a week  and if you do things holding four times  per month then try to do it once a month  and try to apply that to your business  because you get in the zone a little bit  to say I'm on Sam checking email and an  email comes in if I'm working on  something else and I then check my email  it takes me another you know 15 minutes  to get back into what I was doing before  or long ways it's a big distraction or  if you can just go through all your mail  email all at once you're in that mode  you're entering things quickly you're  ready to go on to the next one you're  not being distracted by anything else  and you become a lot more productive so  you can get a lot more done in less time  by focusing your energies on one thing  and one task at a time so my typical day  I'm usually breaking my day down into  three one and a half hour chunks and I  find that one and a half hours is enough  time for me to kind of get something  completely done work really hard and  then take a break because after that my  brain starts to fry a little bit so I'll  break my day in two three one and a half  hour chunks usually from Monday to  Thursday that's what I'll be in the  office and then one of those trunks will  be email so email everything related to  email so if I need to answer the email  log of C but also look at the proposal  or get back to staff members or whatever  it is anything related to email is one  and a half hours per day Monday the  Thursday and I find that really helpful  because it forces me to focus you know  you only have an hour and a half you got  to get it done when you have that fixed  timeline you know you have to actually  you know buckle down get the word not  get distracted by anything else and when  it does is that this whole system allows  you to free up extra time to their do  more work if you want to or also have a  better work-life balance and go out and  do other things that can help you grow  personally professionally so my one and  a half hours email Monday to Thursday  then from there  each day's looks a little bit different  at least for me my monday is usually my  big work day so I try to get everything  done as much as I can for the week on  Monday so you know I may not get to all  the emails that come in on Monday if I  don't have time that one and a half  hours because I haven't checked since  thursday afternoon but then I'm doing  all sorry cough attack if I have client  work or things that are done that are  due during the week creating my  newsletter creating a blog post all that  is done on monday as much as possible so  i'll use the 21 and a half hour chunks  that are remaining on Monday to do that  I try to get everything done as much as  I can so I have the rest of the week to  focus on things i want to focus on  tuesdays usually want to call my CEO day  and so that's when I work on projects  that are undefined so every month is  something different I'm working on  things that I'm trying to use to grow my  business and as much as fall so you want  to make sure you have CEO time built  into every week so that you have time to  focus on the growth part right so you're  not just putting out fires and reacting  but you're able to grow your business on  Wednesday it's my video day so this is  Wednesday i'm filming all my videos i  look at everything that's been that's  come in for the past week and I usually  write back to people say i'll create a  video reply to you and i'll let you know  when it comes up and so on wednesday i  stay at home and i create my videos and  then I send them up to my editor who put  all the visuals and music and all that  fancy stuff in and so that's what i do  on wednesdays and then Thursday is my  meeting day and on Thursdays I'll have  calls and meetings and basically get in  the zone for that is usually at my  office or I call people and I set  everything up kind of back to back for  one day to do that and then friday is  usually off or I'm you know writing my  worksheets or you know don't check don't  check email don't book anything off and  then Friday excited Saturday Sundays off  for the weekend so that's kind of my  typical week and why I find it really  helpful to check your time so say our  meeting for example if you're doing  phone calls or you're meeting people  there's always a little bit of prep time  in advance right like the 15 minutes or  20 minutes before meeting or before  phone call you should is not very  productive right if you know you have a  meet  coming up or especially if somebody's  late on a phone call you can't really  get anything really productive done in  that time because you're thinking about  what's coming up so you can't really do  anything high-level just before that and  often just after that you get ideas that  come from the meeting and so you can't  really focus on anything else afterwards  as well and so I find if you have too  many meetings spread over over various  days you just spent that time in  meetings around phone calls and not  spending time growing your business so I  find that I book the meetings back to  back to back to back we're phone calls  as well and i find that gets me in the  zone so i wake up on thursday i know i'm  gonna have lots of meetings today that's  my meeting day you know have a shower  get changed you know dress up you're  ready to go and basically being the  mindset of going out and talking to  people being friendly outgoing and and  that's my mindset for the day and then  after Thursday I kind of decompress take  all the information and figure what my  next steps are going to be with all the  people that I met we're on a day like  Monday it's my min day to my get  everything done that I need to get done  for the week day I find that it's a  different mindset right I don't have to  worry about going out and talking to  people I'm more introverted on a monday  because i just have to buckle down and  work you know i don't have to dress up  if i don't want to don't have to shave  if i don't want to and so having those  different days i find really helps get  me in the zone for each particular task  and allows me to be a lot more  productive i get a lot more done in that  time in those you know three one and a  half hour chunks a day than i did before  during regular nine-to-five or plus work  hours so it frees up more time that you  can then use if you want to add another  chunk or to do your kind of personal  life stuff as well so hopefully that  helps maybe too much information in the  video i don't know hopefully you guys  liked it the worksheets explain a lot  more but i wanted to try to give you as  much info as I could through the video  it's a great question something I'm  really passionate about is trying to  improve your productivity so if you guys  liked the video please give it a thumbs  up below it makes fun to do more of  these duties for you and you have a  question about my schedule or about this  video or a different question about your  business but for leave in the comments  below I always read those i always reply  so thank you and I'll see you in the  next episode  you
 

